    "readme_description": "You are given a <strong>0-indexed</strong> integer array <code>nums</code>. A pair of indices <code>(i, j)</code> is a <strong>bad pair</strong> if <code>i &lt; j</code> and <code>j - i != nums[j] - nums[i]</code>.\n\nReturn <em>the total number of <strong>bad pairs</strong> in </em><code>nums</code>.",
    "_readme_examples": {
        "list": [
            {
                "content": "```\nInput: nums = [4,1,3,3]\nOutput: 5\n```\n**Explanation:** The pair (0, 1) is a bad pair since 1 - 0 != 1 - 4.\nThe pair (0, 2) is a bad pair since 2 - 0 != 3 - 4, 2 != -1.\nThe pair (0, 3) is a bad pair since 3 - 0 != 3 - 4, 3 != -1.\nThe pair (1, 2) is a bad pair since 2 - 1 != 3 - 1, 1 != 2.\nThe pair (2, 3) is a bad pair since 3 - 2 != 3 - 3, 1 != 0.\nThere are a total of 5 bad pairs, so we return 5."
            },
            {
                "content": "```\nInput: nums = [1,2,3,4,5]\nOutput: 0\n```\n**Explanation:** There are no bad pairs."
            }
        ]
